      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "In 50 patients with a diagnosis of brain metastasis, a study was made commencing with the appearance of the first neurological symptom. Severe headaches were observed in 48% of the patients, followed by a change in character in 11% and motor disorders in 11%. The search for initial neurological signs will help dictate the precise moment of using the scanner to confirm the diagnosis, thus hopefully allowing for a quicker treatment and improving the survival rates of these patients."},
